Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] run the torch, concurrency and conflicts of V4L2 cameras

The cameras a host presents as V4L2 nodes stream together only as their descriptions say, and some
cannot be open beside others. Report the sets of cameras whose concurrency masks agree as the
concurrent streaming combinations (each set is reduced to the cameras that support the guaranteed
stream combinations and reported when two remain), and the cameras a camera's conflict mask names as
its conflicting devices.

The torch is the camera device's flash control and needs no stream: turning it on writes
FLASH_LED_MODE on the camera's capture node, and a camera whose session is blocked (privacy control
set) has no torch: its torch status is not available from the start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
